    "done_when": "Defect (from the crew-observability-truth followup on the lagging pointer field): a live pointer can carry session_id null while its stream's first record already names the session, and the resolver's session_resolution.session_id later recovers it; any reader keying on the raw session_id field sees the run as unresumable during that window, and the standing discard rule treats a null captured session as a lost resume path. First confirm at base, over a temporary run whose pointer has session_id null and whose stream.jsonl opens with a record naming a session, that the recovery classification in reckon/crew/recovery.py reports it as not resumable or recommends discard. Done when that run classifies as resumable, with the recovery naming resume rather than discard; every resumability decision in reckon/crew/recovery.py reads the resolved value (session_resolution) rather than the raw field; a pointer whose stream names no session and whose ledger holds none still classifies as unresumable exactly as before. Reuse the existing session resolver; do not write a second stream parser. Tests in tests/test_crew_recover.py, under a temporary config home with the real config home asserted untouched. At least one added assertion must fail at the dispatch base. Measured over tests/test_crew_recover.py plus tests/test_crew_recovery.py plus tests/test_recovery_state_typing.py in ONE invocation: zero added failures against base. Report ruff findings on the staged paths against the count at base.",
